    #  J. The phase, the script's directory <scratch>/p4, the build directory
    #     <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p3-p4-size (refused if it is already there,
    #     as P3's script did), the commits by their full subjects, and
    #     planning's uncommitted specs/0018 (its sha256 compared with the hash
    #     planning gave, PLANNING_GAVE, default the P4 rulings' 52fcf673... (P4 ruling 5; the fork wrote c00995c9, the hash before it),
    #     with a control).
    #  K. Sixteen probes: part 2's fourteen and the two of this part,
    #     probe-emend-format-write-xml (features emend,xml) and
    #     probe-emend-rowcol-write-xml (the probe crate's feature rowcol, which
    #     turns on emend/rowcol, built alone). The fourteen are compared with
    #     part 2's record, rebuilt at its commit 1fc8327 and reproducing part 2
    #     P3's log's sha256 first; the two are new (P4 ruling 1).
    #  L. The feature evidence of P3's script (change F there), widened: cargo
    #     tree -e features -i emend --charset ascii over size-probe with each
    #     feature set, counted for the feature rowcol: 0 for emend,xml (the
    #     format and every core probe) and for dates, 1 or more for rowcol (the
    #     control), and for emend-copy (the tool that turns it on). The
    #     dependency-tree block adds the rowcol set, which names the same crates
    #     as emend,xml: the feature is emend's own code.
    #  M. The core built with the dates and rowcol features off and on, alone,
    #     on both targets (part 2's block covered dates).
    #  N. The figures block is rebuilt for decision 7 A: the budget on the format
    #     probe against 458752 as the judgment; the part's own cost over the
    #     fullstyles probe; the feature's cost over the format probe; the growth
    #     since part 2's 399176, read from its record's figures table, split
