    ## The release binaries the corpus run uses
    
    `specs/0018-rows-and-columns.md`, "P4", has the corpus run use the binaries
    this log hashed. `emend-copy` and `xlsx-diff` are built in the release
    profile for the host and for i686-unknown-linux-musl in `records/logs/m2p3-p4/size.log`, each
    printed there on a line `hash: <name> <target> <sha256>`, and the run log
    compares the sha256 of what it runs with the one this log printed, reading it
    out of this log by command.
    
    ## Reading these figures
    
    File sizes on this target change in whole 4096-byte steps. They are not
    themselves whole pages: all sixteen probes leave the same remainder, 2596
    bytes, modulo 4096, so it is every DIFFERENCE between them that is a whole
    number of pages. A change under a page is therefore invisible in the file
    size, while the section totals, from `size -A`, resolve to the byte. Both
    are given for every figure above.
